# Part F: Execute the Pig Programs

Assuming Apache Pig is installed and configured to use Hadoop, run these commands from your terminal.

For total views per hour per day:

```bash
pig -x mapreduce hour_day.pig
```

For total views per day:

```bash
pig -x mapreduce views_per_day.pig
```

For total views per hour across all days:

```bash
pig -x mapreduce views_per_hour.pig
```

For word count:

```bash
pig -x mapreduce wordcount.pig
```

The `-x mapreduce` option tells Pig to execute the scripts using Hadoop MapReduce.

